For \(nHitsDedx\) cut efficiency, the distribution from embedding does not describe the real data \(nHitsDedx\) distribution very well. So this efficiency is studied individually with the real data. The efficiency definition is shown in Eq. 4.8. Fig. 4.17 shows the \(nHitsDedx\) cut efficiency.

Figure 4.15: \(\phi\) dependence of TPC tracking efficiency. Upper panels: Run10. Lower panels: Run11.

\[\varepsilon_{nHitsDedx}=\frac{N_{pass\ other\ track\ quality\ cuts+nHitsDedx\ cut}}{N_{pass\ other\ track\ quality\ cuts}} \tag{4.8}\]

