For TPC actually does not cover the fully \(\phi\) range, the dead area between different sectors will effect the TPC tracking efficiency. TOF also has this acceptance bias. So the efficiencies for TPC and TOF are divided into several \(\eta\) and \(\phi\) bins to point this acceptance effect out. This \(\eta\) and \(\phi\) dependence can be found in Fig. 4.15 and Fig. 4.18. This detailed geometry bias of TPC will also effect the acceptance difference between unlike-sign ee pair and like-sign ee pair in the magnetic field. This acceptance difference

